I.	 Bubble Sort:
Definition: Bubble Sort is the simplest sorting algorithm that works by repeatedly swapping the adjacent elements if they are in the wrong order.

Time Complexity: Best case: O(n)
		         Worst Case: O(n2)

Space Complexity: O(1)

Conclusion: Bubble Sort is a simple and easy-to-understand sorting algorithm that repeatedly compares adjacent elements and swaps them if they are in the wrong order.
After each pass, the largest unsorted element moves to its correct position.


